# Cross-platform line endings — HARD REQUIREMENT (Windows + macOS + Linux).
#
# Shell scripts and Python are executed on Windows via Git Bash / python3. A
# CRLF checkout — the Windows default (core.autocrlf=true) — puts a `\r` on
# every line, which breaks bash (`$'\r': command not found`, broken shebang)
# and can corrupt the engine's scripts. That would break EVERY migration,
# sync_engine.sh, install.sh, and the python pipeline for a friend on Windows.
# So every text file the engine ships is normalised to LF on all platforms.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Belt-and-suspenders for the executable/parsed formats that MUST stay LF.
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.py    text eol=lf
*.md    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf
*.json  text eol=lf

# PowerShell (if ever added as the Windows-equivalent of a shell path) is the
# one exception — it prefers CRLF.
*.ps1   text eol=crlf

# Append-only ledgers merge by union. Every scheduler tick appends a line to the
# end of the same file, so two ticks that overlap ALWAYS conflict when the later
# one rebases onto the earlier — and a conflicted rebase delivers nothing, losing
# the whole tick. Union keeps both sides' lines, which is the only correct result
# for a file whose writers never edit or remove a line. Only files that are
# strictly append-only belong here: union on a file that is rewritten (the
# candidate buffers, which lint archives in place) would resurrect removed lines.
zettelkasten/_system/state/tick-telemetry.jsonl          merge=union
zettelkasten/_system/state/agent-lens-runs.jsonl         merge=union
zettelkasten/_system/state/check-decision-runs.jsonl     merge=union
zettelkasten/_system/state/lens-resolution-history.jsonl merge=union
zettelkasten/_system/state/identity-gate.jsonl           merge=union
zettelkasten/_system/roles/*/log.jsonl                   merge=union
